/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (AI transformation is not suffering from a shortage of ambition, investment, or intent. The organisations failing to produce return have approved the budgets, hired the talent, commissioned the programmes, and built the business cases. In many cases they have done all of this more than once. The stall point is consistent. The explanations are familiar. And the investment continues to flow.)
/E (AI transformation is not suffering from a shortage of ambition, investment, or intent. The organisations failing to produce return have approved the budgets, hired the talent, commissioned the programmes, and built the business cases. In many cases they have done all of this more than once. The stall point is consistent. The explanations are familiar. And the investment continues to flow.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (What almost none of these organisations have done is ask the prior question with any precision: does the human layer, the system through which AI investment must pass before it produces enterprise value, have the specific conditions required to make that investment work? Which conditions are in place? Which are weak? And which one is limiting the return on everything built around it?)
/E (What almost none of these organisations have done is ask the prior question with any precision: does the human layer, the system through which AI investment must pass before it produces enterprise value, have the specific conditions required to make that investment work? Which conditions are in place? Which are weak? And which one is limiting the return on everything built around it?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (The human layer is not a homogeneous zone to be warmed up or managed. It has a structure. That structure has six distinct conditions, and those conditions behave in a way that most AI transformation strategy has not accounted for. The consequences are now visible, at scale, across sectors making serious AI investments.)
/E (The human layer is not a homogeneous zone to be warmed up or managed. It has a structure. That structure has six distinct conditions, and those conditions behave in a way that most AI transformation strategy has not accounted for. The consequences are now visible, at scale, across sectors making serious AI investments.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
