/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 70 0 R
/T (The human layer is a transmission layer. Every unit of investment in AI infrastructure, tooling, talent, and deployment passes through it before it produces return. The condition of that layer determines how much of the investment survives the journey from commitment to enterprise value. A well-resourced programme passing through a weak human layer produces the same outcome as an under-resourced programme. The layer is the constraint, not the commitment behind it.)
/E (The human layer is a transmission layer. Every unit of investment in AI infrastructure, tooling, talent, and deployment passes through it before it produces return. The condition of that layer determines how much of the investment survives the journey from commitment to enterprise value. A well-resourced programme passing through a weak human layer produces the same outcome as an under-resourced programme. The layer is the constraint, not the commitment behind it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 70 0 R
/T (The response to this, across programmes and sectors, has been to treat the human layer as a single dial to be turned up. Culture. Engagement. Change management. Skills. Addressed in aggregate, improved in parallel, and monitored with tools \(engagement surveys, skills assessments, technology audits\) that measure each condition independently and say nothing about the relationships between them.)
/E (The response to this, across programmes and sectors, has been to treat the human layer as a single dial to be turned up. Culture. Engagement. Change management. Skills. Addressed in aggregate, improved in parallel, and monitored with tools \(engagement surveys, skills assessments, technology audits\) that measure each condition independently and say nothing about the relationships between them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 70 0 R
/T (This is the most expensive misunderstanding in enterprise AI today. The human layer is not a single dial. These are not six areas to improve in parallel. They are a system, and the output of a system is determined by its most constrained point, not by the average performance of its parts. The argument advanced here is that the six conditions are causally linked and sequentially dependent. The behaviour of a causally linked system is categorically different from the behaviour of six parallel improvement tracks, and investing in one without understanding its relationship to the others is the structural error underlying the majority of stalled AI programmes. The benchmark dataset being built through the founding cohort is what will move this from argued architecture to demonstrated pattern.)
/E (This is the most expensive misunderstanding in enterprise AI today. The human layer is not a single dial. These are not six areas to improve in parallel. They are a system, and the output of a system is determined by its most constrained point, not by the average performance of its parts. The argument advanced here is that the six conditions are causally linked and sequentially dependent. The behaviour of a causally linked system is categorically different from the behaviour of six parallel improvement tracks, and investing in one without understanding its relationship to the others is the structural error underlying the majority of stalled AI programmes. The benchmark dataset being built through the founding cohort is what will move this from argued architecture to demonstrated pattern.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
