/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 71 0 R
/T (In a causally linked system of the kind this model describes, one condition acts as the binding constraint. It is the condition that, left unaddressed, limits the return on everything else invested around it. The organisations generating durable AI advantage are not, in the main, the ones with the largest budgets. From what is observable, they are the ones that identified their most constrained upstream condition and addressed it first. That understanding is not available from intuition, from an engagement survey, or from a technology audit. It requires a different kind of diagnostic entirely.)
/E (In a causally linked system of the kind this model describes, one condition acts as the binding constraint. It is the condition that, left unaddressed, limits the return on everything else invested around it. The organisations generating durable AI advantage are not, in the main, the ones with the largest budgets. From what is observable, they are the ones that identified their most constrained upstream condition and addressed it first. That understanding is not available from intuition, from an engagement survey, or from a technology audit. It requires a different kind of diagnostic entirely.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 71 0 R
/T (In practice, the question of which condition is constraining the system is almost never asked. Investment flows in parallel, on the assumption that the weakest area will benefit most from the most attention. In a sequentially dependent system, that logic does not hold. The constraint remains. The return does not arrive.)
/E (In practice, the question of which condition is constraining the system is almost never asked. Investment flows in parallel, on the assumption that the weakest area will benefit most from the most attention. In a sequentially dependent system, that logic does not hold. The constraint remains. The return does not arrive.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
