/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 72 0 R
/T (The six conditions that constitute the human layer are not abstractions. Each corresponds to a specific and observable failure pattern, consistent enough, across industries, geographies and investment levels, to name precisely. The architecture itself is the result of a structured synthesis: organisational psychology, change implementation research, and direct observation across more than two decades of large-scale transformation programmes, selected for non-overlapping coverage of the human layer and developed against the failure patterns most consistently observed in AI implementations at scale.)
/E (The six conditions that constitute the human layer are not abstractions. Each corresponds to a specific and observable failure pattern, consistent enough, across industries, geographies and investment levels, to name precisely. The architecture itself is the result of a structured synthesis: organisational psychology, change implementation research, and direct observation across more than two decades of large-scale transformation programmes, selected for non-overlapping coverage of the human layer and developed against the failure patterns most consistently observed in AI implementations at scale.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
