/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 72 0 R
/T (The boardroom conversation. The executive team agrees that AI is the strategic priority. The Chief Digital Officer presents the roadmap. The Chief Revenue Officer wants AI for sales acceleration. The Chief Operating Officer wants it for process efficiency. The Chief People Officer wants it for talent. Nobody disagrees. Nobody owns the answer to what AI transformation means at the level of the enterprise, what success looks like when it scales beyond the individual business unit, and what the organisation is actually deploying toward.)
/E (The boardroom conversation. The executive team agrees that AI is the strategic priority. The Chief Digital Officer presents the roadmap. The Chief Revenue Officer wants AI for sales acceleration. The Chief Operating Officer wants it for process efficiency. The Chief People Officer wants it for talent. Nobody disagrees. Nobody owns the answer to what AI transformation means at the level of the enterprise, what success looks like when it scales beyond the individual business unit, and what the organisation is actually deploying toward.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 72 0 R
/T (Eighteen months later, there are pilots. Some are genuinely impressive. None have scaled. The question of why produces different answers from different functions, all of them partial and none of them wrong. The organisation is not uncommitted. It is not under-invested. It has no coherent strategic logic for what AI is for, and that absence makes every downstream decision less productive than it should be. This is the vision vacuum. It is the most upstream failure in the system, and the one that most consistently goes unnamed.)
/E (Eighteen months later, there are pilots. Some are genuinely impressive. None have scaled. The question of why produces different answers from different functions, all of them partial and none of them wrong. The organisation is not uncommitted. It is not under-invested. It has no coherent strategic logic for what AI is for, and that absence makes every downstream decision less productive than it should be. This is the vision vacuum. It is the most upstream failure in the system, and the one that most consistently goes unnamed.)
