/T (In one organisation, the CEO's keynote is compelling and the AI-first commitment is visible and genuine. Two weeks after the all-hands, the same CEO is still running their direct reports' meetings from a printed briefing pack. In another, the board approves a company-wide AI adoption programme while permitting their own function to operate under different expectations. In a third, the transformation agenda is enthusiastically delegated to a Chief Digital Officer, and the leadership layer absents itself entirely from its progress. The specific form matters less than the signal it produces. Every layer of the organisation reads the gap between what transformation requires and what the leadership layer personally demonstrates, and calibrates accordingly. An organisation with clear strategic intent and a leadership layer that does not embody it has a strategy that stops at the boardroom door.)
