132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 74 0 R
/T (This pattern repeats across sectors, organisation types, and geographies with a consistency that rules out programme design as the explanation. What the upskilling initiative could not address, what no training programme is built to address, is the question of identity. The people in that programme had spent ten, twenty, or thirty years building expertise, judgment, and professional craft in a particular way. That expertise is real and valued. It is also built on a foundation that AI now partially displaces. The skills transfer asks people to redesign not just how they work but what their competence means. That is not a learning challenge. It is a conditions challenge. It requires psychological safety to experiment without the risk of looking incompetent in front of colleagues and clients. It requires an organisational environment where identity is not threatened by change but supported through it. Skills without those conditions do not hold. They are acquired in a programme and quietly abandoned when the programme ends, because the deeper conditions for sustained different behaviour were never established.)
/E (This pattern repeats across sectors, organisation types, and geographies with a consistency that rules out programme design as the explanation. What the upskilling initiative could not address, what no training programme is built to address, is the question of identity. The people in that programme had spent ten, twenty, or thirty years building expertise, judgment, and professional craft in a particular way. That expertise is real and valued. It is also built on a foundation that AI now partially displaces. The skills transfer asks people to redesign not just how they work but what their competence means. That is not a learning challenge. It is a conditions challenge. It requires psychological safety to experiment without the risk of looking incompetent in front of colleagues and clients. It requires an organisational environment where identity is not threatened by change but supported through it. Skills without those conditions do not hold. They are acquired in a programme and quietly abandoned when the programme ends, because the deeper conditions for sustained different behaviour were never established.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
