142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 75 0 R
/T (As AI moves from tool to active collaborator in how decisions are made, the conditions governing that collaboration become consequential at an organisational level. The failure runs in both directions. Organisations where AI is used without governance create risk that outpaces the value being generated: liability exposure, accountability gaps, inconsistency that erodes rather than builds confidence. Organisations where governance was designed primarily to prevent risk rather than enable use create a different and equally costly problem. Capable people work carefully around AI rather than genuinely with it, generating the cost of adoption without its value. Neither is a stable position. The organisations producing durable return have built something more specific than a policy: the conditions in which people can trust their own judgement about when and how to use AI, and the organisation can trust theirs.)
/E (As AI moves from tool to active collaborator in how decisions are made, the conditions governing that collaboration become consequential at an organisational level. The failure runs in both directions. Organisations where AI is used without governance create risk that outpaces the value being generated: liability exposure, accountability gaps, inconsistency that erodes rather than builds confidence. Organisations where governance was designed primarily to prevent risk rather than enable use create a different and equally costly problem. Capable people work carefully around AI rather than genuinely with it, generating the cost of adoption without its value. Neither is a stable position. The organisations producing durable return have built something more specific than a policy: the conditions in which people can trust their own judgement about when and how to use AI, and the organisation can trust theirs.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
