/T (For the board member, this is not only a question of organisational performance. It is increasingly a question of governance accountability. Boards are approving AI investment at a scale that warrants the same analytical rigour applied to any other capital allocation decision. The question of whether the human layer is ready to produce return on that investment is a governance question, and it does not yet have a standard answer. There is no established discipline of human layer analytics. No standard methodology for measuring the conditions that determine whether AI investment produces return. That absence reflects how recently the scale of the cost has become visible, and how long it has gone unaddressed.)
