endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Title (What almost none of these organisations have done is ask the prior question with any precision: does the human layer, the system through which AI investment must pass before it produces enterprise value, have the specific conditions required to make that investment work? Which conditions are in place? Which are weak? And which one is limiting the return on everything built around it?)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 167 0 R
/Prev 229 0 R
/Next 291 0 R
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Title (The human layer is not a homogeneous zone to be warmed up or managed. It has a structure. That structure has six distinct conditions, and those conditions behave in a way that most AI transformation strategy has not accounted for. The consequences are now visible, at scale, across sectors making serious AI investments.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 167 0 R
/Prev 290 0 R
/Next 230 0 R
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Title (02 THE TRANSMISSION LAYER)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 230 0 R
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Title (The human layer is a transmission layer. Every unit of investment in AI infrastructure, tooling, talent, and deployment passes through it before it produces return. The condition of that layer determines how much of the investment survives the journey from commitment to enterprise value. A well-resourced programme passing through a weak human layer produces the same outcome as an under-resourced programme. The layer is the constraint, not the commitment behind it.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 231 0 R
/Next 351 0 R
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Title (Where an upstream condition is weak, downstream value is constrained regardless of how well the downstream conditions perform; a pattern consistent enough, across the AI transformation wave so far, to warrant planning against.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 231 0 R
/Prev 352 0 R
/First 353 0 R
/Last 353 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Title (invest seriously in the governance and structural conditions that allow AI to scale, and still see those investments adopted tentatively, worked around, generating cost  without return, because an upstream condition that those investments depend on was never in place. The downstream investment was sound. The upstream constraint made it largely irrelevant.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 231 0 R
/Next 354 0 R
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Title (UPSTREAM FIRST)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 355 0 R
/First 356 0 R
/Last 356 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 232 0 R
>>
endobj
