420 0 obj
<<
/Title (For the board member, this is not only a question of organisational performance. It is increasingly a question of governance accountability. Boards are approving AI investment at a scale that warrants the same analytical rigour applied to any other capital allocation decision. The question of whether the human layer is ready to produce return on that investment is a governance question, and it does not yet have a standard answer. There is no established discipline of human layer analytics. No standard methodology for measuring the conditions that determine whether AI investment produces return. That absence reflects how recently the scale of the cost has become visible, and how long it has gone unaddressed.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 391 0 R
/Prev 408 0 R
/Next 409 0 R
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Title (The boardroom conversation. The executive team agrees that AI is the strategic priority. The Chief Digital Officer presents the roadmap. The Chief Revenue Officer wants AI for sales acceleration. The Chief Operating Officer wants it for process efficiency. The Chief People Officer wants it for talent. Nobody disagrees. Nobody owns the answer to what AI transformation means at the level of the enterprise, what success looks like when it scales beyond the individual business unit, and what the organisation is actually deploying toward.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 400 0 R
/Prev 410 0 R
/Next 411 0 R
>>
