424 0 obj
<<
/Title (An organisation completes a six-month AI upskilling programme. Completion rates are high. Assessment scores are strong. Facilitator feedback is positive. Six months later, the tools are open in browser tabs and used occasionally rather than fluently, applied at the margins of work rather than at its centre. The programme was well-designed. The skills were transferred. The adoption is shallow.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 404 0 R
/Prev 414 0 R
/Next 415 0 R
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Title (Executive sponsorship is visible and genuine. In the teams closest to the work, curiosity about AI is real. Six months into the programme, the transformation has not moved through the organisation. It is not being resisted. It is simply not moving.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 405 0 R
/Prev 416 0 R
/Next 426 0 R
>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<<
/Title (The reason is structural, not cultural. Between the executive intent and the frontline willingness sits a layer of middle management that was not consulted when the strategy was formed, has not been equipped to carry it into their teams, and whose performance metrics have not changed to reflect it. These managers are accountable)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 405 0 R
/Prev 425 0 R
/Next 417 0 R
>>
endobj
